1
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:09,740
(Hwang In Youp)

2
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:14,720
(Lee Hye Ri)

3
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:21,990
(Baek Sung Chul, Lee Yul Eum)

4
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:39,069
(Dream To You)

5
00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:40,169
(All people, events, and backgrounds are fictional.)

6
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:41,179
(This drama includes footage created using AI.)

7
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,180
(Children and animals were filmed under strict safety guidelines.)

8
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:52,790
Why am I on this path standing here?

9
00:00:52,890 --> 00:00:56,690
Is this really my path?

10
00:00:56,760 --> 00:01:00,530
At the end of this path

11
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:03,700
Will my dream come true?

12
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,129
I want to confidently say this is my path

13
00:01:06,130 --> 00:01:08,199
Believe it, and never turn back...

14
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:10,500
- Hey, hey. - Without regret

15
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:17,650
Do you think...

16
00:01:18,410 --> 00:01:20,150
you're walking a straight path right now?

17
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:22,020
Why would you say that?

18
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,290
Are you looking down on me because I got fired?

19
00:01:25,050 --> 00:01:26,520
No, that's not it.

20
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,020
Where are you going? This path you're on, where does it lead?

21
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:31,460
The same path as you.

22
00:01:32,690 --> 00:01:33,690
What?

23
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:35,430
I'm saying I'll make a movie with you.

24
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:51,779
- What am I dreaming? - Hey, hey.

25
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:56,049
- Wait a minute. Wait. - For whom is the dream for?

26
00:01:56,050 --> 00:01:59,820
At the end of this path, my dream

27
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,110
My goodness.

28
00:02:25,650 --> 00:02:26,650
Joo Yi Jae.

29
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:30,480
What's the point of living? What's the point?

30
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:46,800
Gosh.

31
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,100
Ian.

32
00:02:57,650 --> 00:02:58,750
What are you doing?

33
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:03,020
- Someone's outside. - Ian, let's go get some breakfast.

34
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:05,250
In Wook.

35
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:11,290
What's wrong? My goodness.

36
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:12,730
It's cold.

37
00:03:13,190 --> 00:03:14,290
- Gosh. - Gosh.

38
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,360
What was that?

39
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:21,440
Are you in there?

40
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:22,900
You're really something else.

41
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:26,470
- Hey, man, I'm taking a shower. - Go ahead.

42
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:35,050
You must be taking a pretty wild shower.

43
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:38,150
It'd be bad if you collapsed in there alone.

44
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:39,820
Bad for me,

45
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:41,490
and bad for the hotel.

46
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:44,430
It'd be awkward for you too, if that's the last anyone sees of you.

47
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:47,660
No,

48
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:49,830
you might be proud of it.

49
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:51,530
That's right.

50
00:03:52,230 --> 00:03:53,230
See you at the lounge.

51
00:04:26,170 --> 00:04:27,170
What are you thinking?

52
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:31,970
- I don't know where to look. - Look?

53
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:35,740
Your eyes are puffy.

54
00:04:55,430 --> 00:04:56,560
Hey, you...

55
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,170
If you're living with someone, you should've told me.

56
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:01,470
I did.

57
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:03,070
We're not living together.

58
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:05,010
- He's in the room next door. - Gosh.

59
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,240
Don't go. Wait.

60
00:05:06,910 --> 00:05:08,510
Since it seems you don't remember what happened yesterday.

61
00:05:11,350 --> 00:05:12,350
Wait.

62
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:44,750
Usually, in this kind of situation, the woman is the one who runs away.

63
00:05:45,650 --> 00:05:48,020
- But I'm Joo Yi Jae. - Sounds like you rehearsed that.

64
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:52,020
How did I get here?

65
00:05:53,190 --> 00:05:55,820
I remember saying I'd do the movie.

66
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:57,320
I need you to explain what happened after that.

67
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:01,630
Is that where you blacked out?

68
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:03,960
What?

69
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:08,340
I had no idea you were so forward.

70
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:10,700
Forward? Me?

71
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:14,540
What could I possibly have done that was so forward?

72
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:17,640
Yi Jae.

73
00:06:19,050 --> 00:06:20,310
You put your house on the market.

74
00:06:20,650 --> 00:06:21,650
What.

75
00:06:24,750 --> 00:06:27,349
It might be a bit old, but you won't find a better layout.

76
00:06:27,350 --> 00:06:29,020
It's south-facing, so it gets plenty of sun.

77
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:32,559
- Gosh, you must be the tenant. - Hello.

78
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:35,730
I spoke with the landlord. You said we could go ahead and look around.

79
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:39,400
And you even gave me the passcode. I'm so grateful.

80
00:06:39,770 --> 00:06:40,770
I did?

81
00:06:41,170 --> 00:06:43,369
Gosh, I've been running around all morning,

82
00:06:43,370 --> 00:06:45,110
I was so eager to show you this place.

83
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:47,140
- Go on, take a look around. - I'm the one...

84
00:06:47,210 --> 00:06:49,010
- Gosh, of course. - I regret.

85
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,740
Take a look over there and here as well.

86
00:06:52,010 --> 00:06:55,920
- I like this place. - Right? I know. Come over here.

87
00:06:56,780 --> 00:06:57,780
Hello.

88
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,290
- Hello. - Hello.

89
00:07:00,350 --> 00:07:01,989
- Hello. - Hello.

90
00:07:01,990 --> 00:07:04,629
- Hello. - Hello. Hello.

91
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:07,060
Hello. Hello.

92
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:11,500
(Film screenwriting and directing contract)

93
00:07:19,210 --> 00:07:21,810
(Film screenwriting and directing contract)

94
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:27,810
- Yi Jae. - Yes?

95
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:29,580
That seal...

96
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:31,220
Is it heavy?

97
00:07:33,950 --> 00:07:34,960
A little.

98
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:36,760
I was the same way. At my first contract signing.

99
00:07:38,990 --> 00:07:42,830
Then how about we look at it a different way?

100
00:07:45,730 --> 00:07:46,730
This world...

101
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:50,840
It's not a place where you can just disappear without anyone knowing.

102
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:54,210
This story belongs to you.

103
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,140
You started it,

104
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,680
so you're the only one who can finish it.

105
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,080
You write it,

106
00:08:00,650 --> 00:08:01,650
and you direct it.

107
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:06,290
And I'll be with you on that journey.

108
00:08:06,850 --> 00:08:07,850
I will.

109
00:08:08,490 --> 00:08:09,490
All the way to the end.

110
00:08:18,570 --> 00:08:19,930
(Joo Yi Jae)

111
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:22,740
Bravo!

112
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:25,510
So, it finally begins.

113
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:27,940
It's a pleasure to meet you. I'm Seo In Wook.

114
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:29,210
Hello.

115
00:08:29,810 --> 00:08:32,410
So that the two of you can focus solely on writing the screenplay,

116
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,720
I'll do everything I can to support you.

117
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:37,180
- Gosh, thank you. - What about the writer's room?

118
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:39,690
Well... She...

119
00:08:40,450 --> 00:08:41,690
doesn't have a place to live.

120
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:44,060
Hey, why would you tell him that?

121
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:46,060
So that explains why you were at the hotel.

122
00:08:46,430 --> 00:08:49,260
- Pardon? - I saw shoes I didn't recognise.

123
00:08:49,530 --> 00:08:51,230
I'm meeting you for the first time, Yi Jae, but your shoes...

124
00:08:59,770 --> 00:09:00,770
were an old acquaintance.

125
00:09:06,410 --> 00:09:08,720
- I'm sorry. - Nothing to be sorry for.

126
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:10,719
As for the writer's room,

127
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,990
I'm looking at a very quiet house in Bunam City.

128
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:14,590
This guy here keeps insisting on it.

129
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:16,420
I know it might be an inconvenience,

130
00:09:16,490 --> 00:09:18,090
but just until the writer's room is set up,

131
00:09:18,190 --> 00:09:19,190
please stay at the hotel.

132
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:21,160
Gosh, no, that's okay. I can just stay at a friend's place.

133
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:24,500
Gosh, no, I can't allow that. You need to be writing.

134
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,570
- You'd be comfortable at the hotel. - Gosh, okay.

135
00:09:27,770 --> 00:09:29,400
Well, then, I look forward to working with you.

136
00:09:32,270 --> 00:09:33,610
I look forward to working with you too.

137
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:38,250
Okay.

138
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:43,950
Make way. Dong Hyeon is here.

139
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,120
It really brings it to life.

140
00:09:47,850 --> 00:09:49,090
Dong Hyeon, what took you so long?

141
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:51,090
It's because you have a great eye for these things.

142
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:52,190
Great, great. Right?

143
00:09:54,730 --> 00:09:56,730
- PD Gyeong Sun Yeong? - Yes?

144
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,370
- I'm Seo In Wook. - I see.

145
00:10:01,170 --> 00:10:04,400
- But it says Jaden here. - That's me as well.

146
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:06,470
I see. Okay.

147
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:10,110
But why is someone from the film company here to see me?

148
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:13,810
I'm here because Joo Yi Jae hasn't received her final payment yet.

149
00:10:14,050 --> 00:10:15,050
Joo Yi Jae?

150
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:16,680
Wait.

151
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,550
And what's your relationship with her?

152
00:10:18,690 --> 00:10:20,450
She just signed a contract with our company.

153
00:10:21,250 --> 00:10:23,390
In a way, I have you to thank for that.

154
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:25,159
I was in the middle of...

155
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:27,460
desperately trying to get Yi Jae to sign with me.

156
00:10:27,990 --> 00:10:32,430
- Still, this needs to be settled. - What? What contract?

157
00:10:32,830 --> 00:10:33,830
And what's there to settle?

158
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:35,940
It seems there's been some kind of administrative error.

159
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,740
Let me look into it, and I'll get back to you.

160
00:10:38,810 --> 00:10:39,870
Gosh, no. That's all right.

161
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:42,040
You're going to handle that tedious task yourself?

162
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:45,010
I heard you find even your own work to be quite a hassle.

163
00:10:45,110 --> 00:10:48,980
Gosh. This is ridiculous. Is that what Joo Yi Jae is telling people?

164
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:53,920
Gosh, it looks like she's holding a grudge and spreading false rumours.

165
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,790
I'm not like that. You're barking up the wrong tree.

166
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:59,159
Violation of the standard contract, making her be your driver,

167
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:01,730
do your editing, clock in for you, and attend your meetings,

168
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:04,429
on top of giving unfair work orders to a temp,

169
00:11:04,430 --> 00:11:05,970
you also wrongfully terminated her.

170
00:11:09,070 --> 00:11:10,900
My company's legal team is very competent.

171
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,640
So as not to inconvenience you,

172
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:19,110
we've neatly organised everything for you to review.

173
00:11:21,050 --> 00:11:22,050
What are those papers?

174
00:11:25,890 --> 00:11:26,890
This...

175
00:11:46,970 --> 00:11:49,610
Just think of this as a warm-up until you get your own studio.

176
00:11:50,110 --> 00:11:51,480
- Don't push yourself too hard. - No way.

177
00:11:51,910 --> 00:11:53,609
In this amazing work environment,

178
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:54,880
my extinguished artistic soul...

179
00:11:56,150 --> 00:11:57,450
is being rekindled.

180
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:04,760
(One hour later)

181
00:12:05,690 --> 00:12:07,590
I guess it has been out for a while.

182
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,200
Let's fan those embers.

183
00:12:12,730 --> 00:12:14,970
For now, how about we watch some movies?

184
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:17,540
References. Right, they're important.

185
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:25,650
(Ko Sang Yeon)

186
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:30,180
He is never on time.

187
00:12:30,650 --> 00:12:31,650
Here he comes now.

188
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:35,590
Director, Sang Yeon isn't ready yet. If you could just wait a moment...

189
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:36,890
He's already late.

190
00:12:37,390 --> 00:12:40,490
- Why should I wait? - I'm sorry. It's my fault.

191
00:12:41,130 --> 00:12:44,129
Gosh, you always accommodate Oh Ha Na's schedule,

192
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:45,970
so what's the big deal if I'm a little late?

193
00:12:46,070 --> 00:12:49,040
I can get ready during the rehearsal.

194
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:51,440
Just get some kid who looks like me to stand in.

195
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:54,709
Hey, you there. You!

196
00:12:54,710 --> 00:12:57,240
- You in the white shirt. Come here. - Hey, go on. Go.

197
00:13:00,550 --> 00:13:03,920
- Me? - Here, Scene 26.

198
00:13:04,650 --> 00:13:05,990
You'll be my stand-in for the rehearsal.

199
00:13:06,590 --> 00:13:08,590
Ha Na, you're actually early for once.

200
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:17,260
Cut. Okay. Gosh, that was really good.

201
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:20,430
It's just the rehearsal, but I want to use this take.

202
00:13:21,330 --> 00:13:22,540
How long have you been acting?

203
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:24,639
We should work together on my next project.

204
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:25,669
Thank you.

205
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:28,580
You've got the look, and you're great at expressing emotions. Right?

206
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:31,650
Hey, you. Come with me.

207
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:35,080
Go on.

208
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:40,690
Gosh, why is he always like this? Seriously... There he goes again.

209
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:42,520
His movie completely bombed,

210
00:13:42,790 --> 00:13:44,820
- so he's on edge. - Hey, what else is new?

211
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:47,030
- I know, right? - Why's he taking it out on him?

212
00:13:53,570 --> 00:13:54,570
What's this about?

213
00:13:55,870 --> 00:13:58,340
- You were laughing at me? - No, I wasn't.

214
00:13:58,410 --> 00:14:00,470
What? Because I'm an actor...

215
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:02,740
they call box-office poison, you think I'm a joke too?

216
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:06,780
- No, sir. - I can tell by your eyes.

217
00:14:07,150 --> 00:14:08,719
You must've thought this was your big chance, right?

218
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,350
Who do you think you are, trying to take my place?

219
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:11,550
That wasn't my intention.

220
00:14:12,350 --> 00:14:13,949
You're my senior, and you're the one who dumped this on me.

221
00:14:13,950 --> 00:14:16,220
Senior? What makes you think I'm your senior?

222
00:14:17,990 --> 00:14:19,760
That's enough, Mr. Ko Sang Yeon.

223
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:21,960
Mr. Ko Sang Yeon?

224
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:25,600
This guy's got some nerve. Lower your gaze.

225
00:14:29,570 --> 00:14:33,440
- If you're done, I'll be on my way. - Look at this jerk.

226
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:38,650
Who do you think you are, acting so high and mighty?

227
00:14:38,810 --> 00:14:40,350
What, did you find yourself a sugar mama?

228
00:14:40,710 --> 00:14:42,520
Who's got your back?

229
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:44,820
I do. What are you going to do about it?

230
00:14:52,430 --> 00:14:55,030
- Has she lost her mind? - Only a dirty mind would think.

231
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:56,260
What's this?

232
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:58,230
So you two have something?

233
00:14:58,300 --> 00:15:01,770
That's right, we are. Who are you to mess with my friend?

234
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:04,170
Friend? Oh Ha Na, you don't have any friends.

235
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,240
You didn't even go to school.

236
00:15:05,310 --> 00:15:06,810
What do you mean I didn't go to school?

237
00:15:06,870 --> 00:15:08,140
Did you not see "Ha Na's High School?"

238
00:15:08,210 --> 00:15:11,080
- You only worked on filming days. - It was going to school, not work.

239
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:14,780
- If there were cameras, it's work. - Gosh, please. And you?

240
00:15:14,850 --> 00:15:15,950
If you were such a model student,

241
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:17,150
why are there many stories of you from high school?

242
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:19,220
It seems your friends really held a grudge.

243
00:15:19,390 --> 00:15:22,820
- What? - Right. They weren't your friends.

244
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:24,760
They were the victims of your bullying.

245
00:15:27,530 --> 00:15:29,030
I already apologised for that.

246
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,930
It's true what they say. A leopard never changes its spots.

247
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:34,870
You should've left your bullying days behind in school, Sang Yeon.

248
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:37,440
I only graduated from middle school. I dropped out.

249
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:41,740
Like that's something to be proud of, you jerk.

250
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:45,180
Let's go, my friend.

251
00:15:46,210 --> 00:15:48,180
Hey. Get back here. Where do you think you're going?

252
00:15:48,250 --> 00:15:49,250
Come here.

253
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:52,090
Gosh. Hot, it's hot.

254
00:15:52,490 --> 00:15:55,560
That jerk. She didn't put it out all the way. Hey, Manager.

255
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:58,090
Manager, report her. It's hot. Gosh. Hey!

256
00:15:58,220 --> 00:15:59,459
(The Classic)

257
00:15:59,460 --> 00:16:01,560
Then, allow me to escort you.

258
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:07,800
Let's pretend that building over there is a shelter and run for it.

259
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:11,670
One, two, three.

260
00:16:54,950 --> 00:16:55,980
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

261
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:16,420
What? Why did I close my eyes?

262
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:34,670
You want me to keep going?

263
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:38,210
No, that's not it.

264
00:19:39,250 --> 00:19:40,250
No, but...

265
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:44,150
Gosh!

266
00:19:48,390 --> 00:19:49,520
Hey, sleep tight.

267
00:19:50,260 --> 00:19:53,830
- Okay, sleep well. - You too.

268
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:55,060
Okay.

269
00:20:18,850 --> 00:20:21,350
Wait, why is he sleeping here?

270
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:29,660
Not coming in?

271
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:31,360
(In Wook)

272
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:32,870
No, I'm not coming in.

273
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:26,420
- Good morning. - Good morning.

274
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:39,670
Looks like you didn't sleep well.

275
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Right.

276
00:21:45,070 --> 00:21:46,070
Eat up.

277
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:54,210
Is there coffee?

278
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:01,450
(S1. Wolhwajeong)

279
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,570
Think.

280
00:22:19,870 --> 00:22:22,240
(S1. Wolhwajeong, Night)

281
00:22:41,230 --> 00:22:43,160
(I can't think of anything. Absolutely nothing.)

282
00:22:43,230 --> 00:22:45,060
(The only thing I can think about is how I can't think of anything.)

283
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:48,570
Have you eaten?

284
00:22:49,500 --> 00:22:50,740
(You worked hard today.)

285
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:52,000
(Let me know if you need anything.)

286
00:22:52,070 --> 00:22:53,340
(The weather is great today. Do you want to take a walk?)

287
00:22:53,410 --> 00:22:54,670
(Do you want to get lunch together later?)

288
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:55,780
(Are you up?)

289
00:23:06,590 --> 00:23:09,760
Gosh. After I retired,

290
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:12,330
I feel so empty. You know?

291
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:16,360
I'm still in one piece. Why did they force me out?

292
00:23:16,430 --> 00:23:18,630
Tell me about it.

293
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:24,170
Once the younger guys start climbing the ladder, you're old news.

294
00:23:24,240 --> 00:23:27,240
These young jerks today, they're all just...

295
00:23:34,550 --> 00:23:36,020
But that's not always the case.

296
00:23:36,150 --> 00:23:38,780
- Unemployment is through the roof. - Right.

297
00:23:39,050 --> 00:23:41,390
Apparently, a lot of them just bum around.

298
00:23:42,620 --> 00:23:46,090
The problem with kids these days is they've got it too easy.

299
00:23:46,160 --> 00:23:47,530
Hey, stop. Behind you...

300
00:23:57,170 --> 00:24:00,270
It's not that I'm bumming around. I'm just deeply troubled.

301
00:24:11,250 --> 00:24:14,290
Hey, Yu Geon. You know that event we talked about?

302
00:24:14,490 --> 00:24:15,490
Did they find someone for it?

303
00:24:18,660 --> 00:24:20,030
I thought you said you were too busy writing.

304
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:23,400
Yu Geon, will you be in my movie?

305
00:24:23,730 --> 00:24:26,630
You know I hate that more than anything.

306
00:24:27,370 --> 00:24:30,940
And if you're thinking of offering me even a small part, please don't.

307
00:24:31,940 --> 00:24:35,140
- Hello. - Okay, I figured as much.

308
00:24:36,080 --> 00:24:38,610
Don't worry. A small role or whatever,

309
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:40,650
I can't even play my own part.

310
00:24:41,610 --> 00:24:43,950
Rather than stare at my desk and not write a single word,

311
00:24:44,180 --> 00:24:45,650
I came out here to make at least some money.

312
00:24:47,420 --> 00:24:49,490
What does Su Bin say?

313
00:24:49,890 --> 00:24:51,390
I'm avoiding him because I'm scared of what he'll say.

314
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:53,530
What am I going to do?

315
00:24:53,990 --> 00:24:57,160
I keep telling myself, "It's no big deal," but I can't calm down.

316
00:24:57,500 --> 00:24:59,970
Just looking at the blinking cursor makes my heart pound like crazy.

317
00:25:00,700 --> 00:25:03,500
And most of all, I'm afraid of disappointing Su Bin.

318
00:25:03,570 --> 00:25:04,870
That's what I'm most afraid of.

319
00:25:06,210 --> 00:25:07,610
I guess you want to impress him.

320
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:11,680
Well, good luck.

321
00:25:24,890 --> 00:25:25,960
Joo Yi Jae.

322
00:25:35,070 --> 00:25:36,070
Joo Yi Jae.

323
00:26:03,500 --> 00:26:04,600
What are you doing? Get in.

324
00:26:21,250 --> 00:26:22,480
Have you seen the comments?

325
00:26:22,550 --> 00:26:23,780
(Oh Ha Na and Ko Sang Yeon seem to have a terrible relationship.)

326
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:26,320
Do you think the viewers are idiots?

327
00:26:26,390 --> 00:26:28,950
They're saying it's obvious you two don't get along.

328
00:26:29,260 --> 00:26:31,860
Kicking him in the shins? Burning you with a cigarette?

329
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:34,490
Do I really have to hear that kind of nonsense from Hyeon Gu?

330
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,960
And who is Hyeon Gu?

331
00:26:36,630 --> 00:26:38,030
The CEO of Ko Sang Yeon's agency.

332
00:26:38,600 --> 00:26:41,470
Please, stop getting into pointless fights with Ko Sang Yeon.

333
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,670
Knowing how to handle your co-stars is a skill too.

334
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:45,739
Gosh. How come every time you're in a romantic comedy,

335
00:26:45,740 --> 00:26:47,310
you're at war with your male leads?

336
00:26:47,410 --> 00:26:50,940
They try to eat me alive, so I have to stop them.

337
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:52,909
- What? - They act like kings.

338
00:26:52,910 --> 00:26:53,980
That's annoying.

339
00:26:54,910 --> 00:26:56,480
But you know what's even more annoying?

340
00:26:57,450 --> 00:27:00,349
That to everyone else, I probably look just as bad as they do.

341
00:27:00,350 --> 00:27:03,260
So what? You could all just enjoy life up in the clouds together.

342
00:27:03,390 --> 00:27:05,620
Why do you insist on coming down to earth?

343
00:27:05,930 --> 00:27:08,990
And Ha Na, saying that on our way to a luxury brand event...

344
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:10,360
Isn't that a little hypocritical?

345
00:27:13,330 --> 00:27:14,469
- Director Kang. - Yes.

346
00:27:14,470 --> 00:27:17,500
- Drop me at the next intersection. - The next intersection. Gosh...

347
00:27:18,070 --> 00:27:21,440
- There. Right there. - We're in the far lane... I'll try.

348
00:27:31,780 --> 00:27:34,350
Hello. From Boers. Would you like to try a sample?

349
00:27:34,990 --> 00:27:35,990
Thank you.

350
00:27:36,190 --> 00:27:38,620
Hello, from Boers. Would you like to try a sample?

351
00:27:42,030 --> 00:27:43,130
Thank you.

352
00:27:44,530 --> 00:27:45,900
Hello, from Boers...

353
00:27:49,270 --> 00:27:50,400
Why aren't you giving me one?

354
00:27:53,410 --> 00:27:56,010
- Pretend you're glad to see me. - But I'm not.

355
00:27:56,440 --> 00:27:57,840
Are you ever going to learn some manners?

356
00:27:57,910 --> 00:27:58,940
Depends on how you behave.

357
00:28:04,320 --> 00:28:05,320
I'm so glad to see her though.

358
00:28:11,060 --> 00:28:12,120
What's this all about?

359
00:28:13,230 --> 00:28:14,230
Are you his manager?

360
00:28:16,330 --> 00:28:19,900
- You? My manager? - No, the other way around.

361
00:28:20,030 --> 00:28:22,770
- Gosh, me? - That's a little casual, isn't it?

362
00:28:22,940 --> 00:28:24,000
And what you just said wasn't?

363
00:28:25,770 --> 00:28:27,769
For someone who's so fluent in Korean,

364
00:28:27,770 --> 00:28:29,910
I wonder why you only babbled in English at the audition.

365
00:28:29,980 --> 00:28:32,680
That was in the US. This is Korea.

366
00:28:35,350 --> 00:28:36,880
Yu Geon, are you and the director friends?

367
00:28:37,020 --> 00:28:39,220
No. You can tell he's older than me.

368
00:28:39,490 --> 00:28:42,450
We were just neighbours for a while when we were kids.

369
00:28:43,060 --> 00:28:44,060
Neighbours?

370
00:28:44,760 --> 00:28:45,760
For a while?

371
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:47,430
Never be friends with him.

372
00:28:53,530 --> 00:28:55,330
- Ha Na! - Ha Na!

373
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:02,780
What's your relationship with her?

374
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:04,080
Curious?

375
00:29:04,410 --> 00:29:07,680
- Yes. - I'm a director, she's an actress,

376
00:29:08,150 --> 00:29:09,150
so what do you think our relationship is?

377
00:29:10,420 --> 00:29:11,580
We're not "neighbours," that's for sure.

378
00:29:12,990 --> 00:29:14,320
Hey, wrong way.

379
00:29:15,050 --> 00:29:16,420
How would you know where I was going?

380
00:29:16,620 --> 00:29:18,590
Just buy one for me.

381
00:29:19,020 --> 00:29:20,660
- Will you give me a discount? - Of course.

382
00:29:22,090 --> 00:29:23,099
All right.

383
00:29:23,100 --> 00:29:24,530
You all love Rube, don't you?

384
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:26,370
- Yes. - You love Rube, don't you?

385
00:29:26,430 --> 00:29:28,270
- Yes. - Who loves it? Who loves it?

386
00:29:29,670 --> 00:29:31,870
If you love Rube, make some noise.

387
00:29:33,970 --> 00:29:35,239
All right, next up...

388
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:39,079
is the moment you've all been waiting for, the lucky draw.

389
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:40,610
That's what's next up.

390
00:29:42,450 --> 00:29:46,850
For this lucky draw, our brand ambassador, actress Oh Ha Na,

391
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:51,560
will be drawing the winners herself. And now, let's bring...

392
00:29:51,620 --> 00:29:55,260
actress Oh Ha Na up to the stage. Come in, Ms. Oh Ha Na.

393
00:30:03,940 --> 00:30:05,840
Yes. It's not often I get a chance...

394
00:30:05,900 --> 00:30:07,340
to meet my fans this up close,

395
00:30:07,410 --> 00:30:09,980
so I hope we all have a wonderful time today.

396
00:30:12,310 --> 00:30:14,680
Who will be our lucky winner?

397
00:30:16,780 --> 00:30:18,820
- It's number 38. - Number 38.

398
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:20,490
That's me. Number 38!

399
00:30:25,360 --> 00:30:26,529
Next is number four.

400
00:30:26,530 --> 00:30:30,960
Number 4. Who's number 4? Number 4. Congratulations.

401
00:30:32,670 --> 00:30:35,000
And now for our last winner, our last one,

402
00:30:35,130 --> 00:30:38,700
- our last, last... - The Last one.

403
00:30:38,770 --> 00:30:42,440
Who wants this one? Raise your hand. Let me see your hands. Hands.

404
00:30:52,020 --> 00:30:53,620
Gosh, my goodness.

405
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:45,070
I'm so sorry.

406
00:31:47,510 --> 00:31:50,910
- Who are you? Do I know you? - One is what I wanted to get you,

407
00:31:52,010 --> 00:31:53,210
and the other is what I was pressured into buying.

408
00:31:54,310 --> 00:31:58,180
- Now I see why he did that. - No, I'm asking, do you know me?

409
00:31:59,280 --> 00:32:02,390
I know who you are, and I know why you're here.

410
00:32:10,160 --> 00:32:12,100
You fool. This is when you should be getting angry.

411
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:20,870
You finally worked up the courage.

412
00:32:22,840 --> 00:32:24,810
You must have been frustrated when things didn't go your way.

413
00:32:26,350 --> 00:32:27,850
You must have been terrified.

414
00:32:29,210 --> 00:32:30,620
But that's perfectly normal.

415
00:32:34,590 --> 00:32:36,390
I get scared too, thinking this might all just be...

416
00:32:37,360 --> 00:32:38,360
my own selfish ambition.

417
00:32:39,020 --> 00:32:42,290
I constantly wonder if I'm just making things harder for you.

418
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:48,170
But we're trying to do something great here.

419
00:32:53,340 --> 00:32:54,340
Yi Jae.

420
00:32:55,840 --> 00:32:57,580
Creating something magnificent...

421
00:32:59,310 --> 00:33:00,310
isn't what makes it great.

422
00:33:03,950 --> 00:33:05,350
The fact that we see it through to the end,

423
00:33:06,490 --> 00:33:07,590
that's what makes it great.

424
00:33:14,390 --> 00:33:15,790
We're going to the studio tomorrow.

425
00:33:17,400 --> 00:33:18,400
Think it over.

426
00:33:19,060 --> 00:33:21,170
Whether you're going to see this through with me or not.

427
00:33:25,600 --> 00:33:26,610
I'm leaving.

428
00:34:07,310 --> 00:34:10,380
Creating something magnificent isn't what makes it great.

429
00:34:13,090 --> 00:34:14,350
The fact that we see it through to the end,

430
00:34:15,620 --> 00:34:16,660
that's what makes it great.

431
00:35:16,680 --> 00:35:17,680
Okay.

432
00:35:30,330 --> 00:35:31,360
Su Bin!

433
00:35:32,630 --> 00:35:34,270
It is you, right?

434
00:35:36,200 --> 00:35:40,140
Gosh. That was close. I've been looking all over for you.

435
00:35:40,740 --> 00:35:41,810
You're late.

436
00:35:42,370 --> 00:35:43,380
The trunk.

437
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:44,880
Okay.

438
00:35:52,350 --> 00:35:53,350
I'll get it.

439
00:36:03,260 --> 00:36:05,960
- Let's go do something great. - Okay.

440
00:36:09,330 --> 00:36:10,770
Gosh.

441
00:36:13,710 --> 00:36:17,210
This is so nice, right? It's amazing.

442
00:36:17,980 --> 00:36:18,980
It really does.

443
00:36:29,250 --> 00:36:33,090
- But I'm fine with anything. - I know this really great place.

444
00:36:33,360 --> 00:36:35,990
Bibimbap. As long as it's not bibimbap.

445
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,800
- Let's get something else then. - Gosh.

446
00:36:38,930 --> 00:36:41,329
Hey, do you remember this place? Over there.

447
00:36:41,330 --> 00:36:42,669
Oh, there?

448
00:36:42,670 --> 00:36:45,640
- You don't remember, do you? - Of course I do. Why wouldn't I?

449
00:37:34,690 --> 00:37:35,790
Hey, you...

450
00:37:37,920 --> 00:37:39,760
- Mom. - What?

451
00:37:40,560 --> 00:37:42,090
What do you want me to be, Mom?

452
00:37:42,660 --> 00:37:43,860
A decent human being.

453
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:46,130
- Same here. - Gosh.

454
00:37:46,870 --> 00:37:49,600
- Stop joking around. - Whatever.

455
00:37:50,640 --> 00:37:52,540
Am I asking what's for dinner?

456
00:37:54,010 --> 00:37:56,140
At least with dinner, I can choose what I want.

457
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:59,440
But I can't get my own kids to do what I want.

458
00:38:00,480 --> 00:38:04,150
A treasure? My pride and joy? Please. Don't make me laugh.

459
00:38:05,950 --> 00:38:07,790
That's harsh to say to your daughter who just got fired.

460
00:38:07,820 --> 00:38:10,720
You were always struggling anyway. I was hoping you'd quit.

461
00:38:10,790 --> 00:38:11,790
It's for the best.

462
00:38:11,920 --> 00:38:13,760
It's not like that was the only place you could work.

463
00:38:14,090 --> 00:38:18,230
You can make a living just by going to festivals all over the country.

464
00:38:18,900 --> 00:38:21,570
Just go buy a car. Stop taking the bus everywhere.

465
00:38:23,570 --> 00:38:24,570
Mom.

466
00:38:25,940 --> 00:38:27,410
I came back here to write.

467
00:38:29,270 --> 00:38:30,280
What did you say?

468
00:38:30,580 --> 00:38:32,810
I'm going to try making movies again.

469
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:38,650
I thought you were over this, but here we go again.

470
00:38:39,380 --> 00:38:40,820
How many times do I have to tell you?

471
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:42,490
That kind of thing is for rich people.

472
00:38:42,620 --> 00:38:44,760
People who live without a care in the world.

473
00:38:46,630 --> 00:38:48,790
So is that why Woo Su Bin made it and I didn't?

474
00:38:49,290 --> 00:38:50,300
Exactly.

475
00:38:51,130 --> 00:38:53,500
And look, he even went to the US and became successful.

476
00:38:53,730 --> 00:38:56,200
His father was against it, so he cut ties with him.

477
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:58,069
You can only have that kind of courage...

478
00:38:58,070 --> 00:38:59,870
when you have something to fall back on.

479
00:39:02,210 --> 00:39:05,380
No wonder I'm in this position. Forget it. I'll live my own life.

480
00:39:10,750 --> 00:39:12,549
Don't tell me you're doing this because of Su Bin.

481
00:39:12,550 --> 00:39:15,450
We already signed the contract. I'm going to work with him.

482
00:39:15,950 --> 00:39:17,919
This girl... Are you out of your mind?

483
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:18,920
Is this some kind of joke?

484
00:39:19,260 --> 00:39:23,060
You can't work with him. After everything he put you through?

485
00:39:23,230 --> 00:39:25,530
Why? It was because he's rich and I'm poor.

486
00:39:25,600 --> 00:39:26,730
What did he do wrong?

487
00:39:27,330 --> 00:39:29,429
If what you say is true, I shouldn't have just gotten off the bus.

488
00:39:29,430 --> 00:39:30,670
I should've left home, right?

489
00:39:31,040 --> 00:39:32,040
I should've forgotten family and everything else.

490
00:39:32,041 --> 00:39:33,540
I should have just lived my own life.

491
00:39:34,870 --> 00:39:36,310
Hey, what's that supposed to mean?

492
00:40:03,840 --> 00:40:07,070
Joo Yi Jae, come out. You little brat.

493
00:40:08,540 --> 00:40:09,540
Come and eat.

494
00:40:25,620 --> 00:40:26,629
(Interbank transfer from...)

495
00:40:26,630 --> 00:40:28,290
(Jung Myung Ja, 100,000 dollars, Deposit)

496
00:40:35,100 --> 00:40:37,040
Gosh! You scared me.

497
00:40:38,100 --> 00:40:39,870
- When did you get here? - Early this morning.

498
00:40:40,070 --> 00:40:41,070
Why?

499
00:40:42,370 --> 00:40:43,380
Ran away.

500
00:40:44,780 --> 00:40:45,780
What?

501
00:40:51,780 --> 00:40:54,290
Anyway, our job is to adapt the original draft.

502
00:40:54,850 --> 00:40:56,119
Taking a decade-old draft...

503
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:57,859
and viewing it with a modern perspective,

504
00:40:57,860 --> 00:40:59,020
reconstructing it will be more complicated than you think.

505
00:40:59,820 --> 00:41:01,860
To save time, we need to nail down the structure first.

506
00:41:02,190 --> 00:41:03,630
So I broke it down into chapters...

507
00:41:04,030 --> 00:41:07,670
- and then outlined the scene order. - Gosh, when did you do all this?

508
00:41:07,770 --> 00:41:08,930
Whenever I had time at the hotel.

509
00:41:09,200 --> 00:41:10,900
Gosh. And you called it a warm-up.

510
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:13,710
From now on, even if we revise dialogue or change the scene order,

511
00:41:13,770 --> 00:41:15,070
this framework will hold up.

512
00:41:17,280 --> 00:41:21,449
But are we really going to work like this? Word for word,

513
00:41:21,450 --> 00:41:24,020
- sharing every comma and period? - Yes.

514
00:41:28,950 --> 00:41:29,960
Really?

515
00:41:30,360 --> 00:41:33,630
This is so embarrassing. It's too raw.

516
00:41:34,490 --> 00:41:37,529
It's not a diary, so what does it matter? This is more efficient.

517
00:41:37,530 --> 00:41:39,200
We can make adjustments as we go in real time.

518
